{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pushed as Gerrit change 1708 (commit 6c62cfb9ff, https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1708).\n\nFull local gate set green before push: make lint, make typecheck (518 files), all argument-less check_* gates exit 0, check_complexity_baseline.py --check = active=55 new=0 increased=0 stale=0, all four generators no-diff, and the CI-parity suite (pytest -m 'not integration and not external' -n 3 --dist worksteal --timeout=300) = 12622 passed, 52 skipped, exit 0.\n\nNote on the baseline diff: it is a pure 4-line DELETION, not a lowering. All four functions fell below the C901 threshold of 15 entirely (measured <= 7), so --update-stale drained their entries. Per .github/complexity-baseline.README.md, removing an entry is an allowed shrink-only change, so the lock gate should accept it. Sibling b2bb (compact split) also regenerates this file; if it lands first the rebase will need a re-run of --update-stale, which is the epic's expected landing-order behavior, not a defect."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786601814223966001,"uuid":"8d934494-dac6-4f86-b328-9136106a1b00"}